GEMINI.md
AGENTS.md
# agent-docs/ was a single repo-wide segment match. It also excluded this repository's own chain
# artifacts. Those are authored records, not build output. state-template.md tells a resuming
# session to trust state.md and `git log` together, which a file git never sees cannot satisfy,
# and DOFLOW_CHAIN.md puts a repository's tier-2 constitution at agent-docs/constitution.md.
# Split so each rule states which of the two it is for.
agent-docs/

# Skill-eval corpus is TRACKED — runner, per-skill eval definitions, and the sanitized baseline —
# so the behavioral baseline is reproducible from a clean clone (review R6, re-landed by feature
# 028 after 97f870a reverted it with no recorded reason). Only run transcripts, disposable
# sandboxes, and generated reports stay local: they are artifacts of paid runs, not corpus.
# config.json is tracked too — its pinned model is a deliberate comparability constraint (FR-017),
# not machine-local state. A blanket bench/ rule here is what let the corpus go local-only twice;
# test/guards/evals.test.js now fails if the corpus stops being present.
bench/runs/
bench/reports/
.mcp.json

# MkDocs build output
site/

# Python bytecode — do-code-review bundles Python analyzers under
# core/shared/skills/do-code-review/scripts/, so importing or byte-compiling one
# leaves artifacts inside the shipped tree
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
/CLAUDE.md

# graphify: generated code-graph index, rebuilt on demand with `graphify update .`
graphify-out/
